---
source: crates/kubelint_linter/src/rules/tests.rs
expression: check_fixture(rule)
---
error[KL1010]: label value `team@example.com` of `owner` is invalid: a valid label must be an empty string or consist of alphanumeric characters, '-', '_' or '.', and must start and end with an alphanumeric character (e.g. 'MyValue', 'my_value' or '12345')
 --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:8:12
  |
8 |     owner: team@example.com
  |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: use letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `team-example.com`; free text belongs in an annotation

error[KL1010]: label key `Team Name` is invalid: its name part must be made of letters, digits, '-', '_' and '.', starting and ending with a letter or digit
 --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:9:5
  |
9 |     Team Name: payments
  |     ^^^^^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `Team-Name`

error[KL1010]: label `version` has a value that YAML reads as a number, not a string
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:10:14
   |
10 |     version: 1.0
   |              ^^^
  = help: quote the value: `version: "1.0"`

error[KL1010]: label `canary` has a value that YAML reads as a boolean, not a string
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:11:13
   |
11 |     canary: yes
   |             ^^^
  = help: quote the value: `canary: "yes"`

error[KL1010]: label key `Example.com/tier` is invalid: its prefix must be a lowercase RFC 1123 subdomain (lowercase letters, digits, '-' and '.', starting and ending with a letter or digit)
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:20:5
   |
20 |     Example.com/tier: web
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `example.com/tier`

error[KL1010]: label key `a/b/c` is invalid: a qualified name must consist of a name with an optional DNS subdomain prefix and '/' (e.g. 'example.com/MyName')
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:21:5
   |
21 |     a/b/c: x
   |     ^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `app.kubernetes.io/name`

error[KL1010]: label key `example.com/` is invalid: its name part must be non-empty
  --> correctness/KL1010.yaml:22:5
   |
22 |     example.com/: x
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: write the key as an optional lowercase DNS prefix and `/`, then up to 63 letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.`, for example `app.kubernetes.io/name`

